WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:05.100
MeetRec records your meetings, and knows who said what.

00:06.000 --> 00:12.200
When a Google Meet, Teams, or Slack huddle starts, it offers to record, right from the menu bar.

00:12.800 --> 00:22.700
Afterwards, every line of the transcript is labeled with its speaker: you, and everyone else on the call.

00:23.300 --> 00:29.200
See how long each person talked, at a glance.

00:29.800 --> 00:35.600
Click a person to see every turn they spoke.

00:35.800 --> 00:42.700
Pick one, and playback jumps right to that moment.

00:43.300 --> 00:46.600
Then ask the AI you already use.

00:46.800 --> 00:52.600
MeetRec talks to Claude Code or Codex, right on your Mac.

00:52.800 --> 00:59.700
It uses your own login, so there's no extra API key.

01:00.300 --> 01:07.700
Transcription runs on your Mac by default, or in the cloud with your own Groq or OpenAI key.

01:08.800 --> 01:12.900
Free and open source, for macOS 15 and later on Apple Silicon.

01:13.100 --> 01:16.800
Get it at meetrec.dorara.app.
